Mood Journal Backend
This backend application allows users to create accounts, record their moods, and track mood analytics over time.
Users can view overall, monthly, and yearly mood reports, calculated as percentages, making it easy to visualize trends with graphs or pie charts on the frontend.

🚀 Features
User Authentication: Secure JWT‑based login and signup.

CRUD Operations: Create, read, update, and delete journal entries.

Mood Analytics:

Overall Analytics – percentage breakdown of all moods recorded.

Yearly Analytics – filter moods by year with percentage distribution.

Monthly Analytics – filter moods by month (YYYY-MM) with percentage distribution.

Secure Data Flow: Each user can only access their own entries.

Database: Built with Sequelize ORM and MySQL.

🛠 Tech Stack
Backend Framework: Express.js

Database: MySQL with Sequelize ORM

Authentication: JWT (JSON Web Token)

Migrations: Sequelize CLI for schema management

📦 Installation
Clone the repository:

Install dependencies:

bash
npm install
Configure your database in config/config.json or .env.

Run migrations:

bash
npx sequelize-cli db:migrate
Start the server:

bash
npm start
🔑 API Routes
Authentication
POST /api/auth/signup – Register a new user

POST /api/auth/login – Login and receive JWT

Journal Entries
POST /api/journel/entry – Create a new journal entry

GET /api/journel/your-moods – Get all journal entries for the logged‑in user

PUT /api/journel/update/:id – Update a journal entry

Mood Analytics
GET /api/mood-analytics/overall-analytics – Get overall mood percentages

GET /api/mood-analytics/yearly-analytics/:year – Get yearly mood analytics

GET /api/mood-analytics/monthly-analytics/:month – Get monthly mood analytics


